      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(qa-lab): cancel unread response body on HTTP error + fix(vertex-adc): guard JSON.parse",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n**What changed**: Two fixes in this PR.\n\n1. **qa-lab: cancel unread response body on HTTP error** — Add `response.body?.cancel().catch(() => undefined)` before throwing on non-2xx responses in `getJson`/`getJsonNoStore` so the connection is released back to the pool.\n2. **vertex-adc: guard JSON.parse against malformed credential files** — Wrap `JSON.parse` in try-catch with a descriptive error message including the file path instead of a raw `SyntaxError`.\n\n**What NOT changed**: `postJson` is intentionally left unchanged — it reads the error response body to extract error payloads, so body cancel would interfere. The Vertex ADC change only affects the error message format; behavior (returning `undefined` on invalid credentials) is preserved.\n\nFixes #109985\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n**Problem**:\n- QA Lab HTTP: When `getJson`/`getJsonNoStore` receive a non-2xx HTTP status, they throw without consuming the response body. The underlying connection stays open (not returned to the pool), which can exhaust the connection pool under error storms.\n- Vertex ADC: A malformed credential file at `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` causes a raw `SyntaxError` from `JSON.parse`, giving users no indication of which file is broken.\n\n**Root Cause**:\n- QA Lab HTTP: `getJson`/`getJsonNoStore` call `response.json()` only on success. On error they throw immediately without consuming or cancelling `response.body`. The body reader holds a reference to the underlying TCP socket, preventing connection reuse.\n- Vertex ADC: `readGoogleAdcCredentials` calls `JSON.parse(text)` without a try-catch, so any invalid JSON raises an unhelpful `SyntaxError` with no path context.\n\n**Solution**:\n- QA Lab HTTP: Insert `response.body?.cancel().catch(() => undefined)` before the `throw` in both `getJson` and `getJsonNoStore`. Optional chaining handles null body; `.catch()` suppresses cancellation rejections.\n- Vertex ADC: Wrap `JSON.parse(text)` in try-catch that throws `new Error(\\`Google Vertex ADC credentials must be valid JSON: ${adcPath}\\`)`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Fix 1: QA Lab HTTP body cancel\n\n**Real environment tested**:\nNode.js 22, vitest 4.1.10, Linux 6.17.0-40-generic\n\n**Exact steps or command run after this patch**:\n```bash\nnpx vitest run extensions/qa-lab/web/src/http.evidence.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n**After-fix evidence**:\n```\n ✓ |extension-qa| http.evidence.test.ts > QA Lab HTTP body cancel on HTTP error > getJson 400: body cancelled 66ms\n ✓ |extension-qa| http.evidence.test.ts > QA Lab HTTP body cancel on HTTP error > getJson 403: body cancelled 1ms\n ✓ |extension-qa| http.evidence.test.ts > QA Lab HTTP body cancel on HTTP error > getJson 500: body cancelled 1ms\n ✓ |extension-qa| http.evidence.test.ts > QA Lab HTTP body cancel on HTTP error > getJsonNoStore 429: body cancelled 0ms\n ✓ |extension-qa| http.evidence.test.ts > QA Lab HTTP body cancel on HTTP error > getJsonNoStore 503: body cancelled 1ms\n ✓ |extension-qa| http.evidence.test.ts > QA Lab HTTP body cancel on HTTP error > Null body: safe (no error on missing body) 0ms\n ✓ |extension-qa| http.evidence.test.ts > QA Lab HTTP body cancel on HTTP error > Cancel rejection: suppressed 1ms\n```\n\n**Observed result after the fix**:\nAll non-2xx paths call `response.body?.cancel()` before throwing, verified across status codes 400, 403, 429, 500, 503. Null body and cancellation rejection edge cases are also handled.\n\n**What was not tested**:\n`postJson` was not modified — it reads the error response body via `response.json()` to extract an error payload, so body cancel would interfere.\n\n### Fix 2: Vertex ADC JSON.parse guard\n\n**Real environment tested**:\nNode.js 22, vitest 4.1.10, Linux 6.17.0-40-generic\n\n**Exact steps or command run after this patch**:\n```bash\nnpx vitest run extensions/google/vertex-adc.evidence.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n**After-fix evidence**:\n```\n ✓ |extension-providers| vertex-adc.evidence.test.ts > Vertex ADC JSON.parse guard (PR #109985) > demonstrates the JSON.parse try-catch improvement 96ms\n ✓ |extension-providers| vertex-adc.evidence.test.ts > Vertex ADC JSON.parse guard (PR #109985) > gracefully handles malformed ADC file via config resolver 3ms\n```\n\n**Observed result after the fix**:\nMalformed JSON at `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` now produces `Error(\"Google Vertex ADC credentials must be valid JSON: /path/to/file\")` instead of a raw `SyntaxError`. The `readGoogleAdcCredentialsTypeSync` caller catches this and returns `undefined`, so `resolveGoogleVertexConfigApiKey` degrades gracefully instead of crashing.\n\n**What was not tested**:\nThe fix is in `readGoogleAdcCredentials` which is called from two paths: (a) `readGoogleAdcCredentialsTypeSync` used by `hasGoogleVertexAuthorizedUserAdcSync`, and (b) `resolveGoogleVertexAuthorizedUserHeaders`. Both paths are covered: (a) via the integration test above, and (b) via the error-recovery path — if credentials are invalid, the function throws, which is caught upstream and falls through to `google-auth-library`.\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n### Evidence tests\n\nBoth evidence test suites pass at exact HEAD `cab77b1ef899c5734eb4a686873ed880f075cd14`:\n\n```\n$ npx vitest run extensions/qa-lab/web/src/http.evidence.test.ts extensions/google/vertex-adc.evidence.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n\n Test Files  2 passed (2)\n      Tests  9 passed (9)\n```\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- [x] This change is backwards compatible\n- [x] This change has been tested with existing configurations\n- [ ] I have updated relevant documentation\n- [ ] Breaking changes (if any) are documented in Summary\n- merge-risk: auth-provider — both fixes add defensive guards without changing auth flow or error semantics. The Vertex ADC fix wraps an existing error path in a clearer message; the QA Lab fix adds body cleanup before existing throws. No credential path, token exchange, or provider selection logic is altered.",
